# W-T1b: the second half of W-T1 - A4 (chained synthetic sessions) and A5 (the thinking-off pair of A1 turns).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-T1 tau lab (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/tau-lab and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time and the data directory is a path under the
# runner's home. Every value is final. ORDER.txt says where it sits in the window.
# W-T1 (Linear THA-268 tooling, THA-269 the run; tau-on-tt design section 1): Qwen3.8-27B's own greedy answers on agent turns, per seat,
# through the PRODUCTION arithmetic: image tp4-serve-2, profile c2-packed-tp4 with the verify T1/T2 audits ON (the run is labelled
# non-production when the image or the audits differ), plus two arithmetic-neutral log flags (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_AUDIT,
# QWEN_FAST_PHASE_TIMING) in a derived profile. ONE container load for every arm, four cards (TP4):
#   A1 SWE-rebench held-out turns (240), A2 our own Claude Code and Codex turns (96, rig-local data), A3 calibration (the lanes 4 x 4k +
#   4 x 32k prompts, built from the image itself, four at once, thinking OFF, 2400 output tokens as the v162/v179 runs had; must
#   reproduce the reference tau the report derives from those runs' logs within +/-7%), A4 chained synthetic agent sessions (20 x 6,
#   the model's own answers fed back, grown to 16k-60k), A5 the thinking-OFF pair of 100 A1 turns. A1, A2 and A4 run thinking ON (the
#   chat template's default, what production agents send); A3 and A5 are thinking OFF (the comparison arms).
# Thinking-ON answers reason first: A1, A2, A4 and A5 get 2048 output tokens each (the default; C2_TAULAB_MAX_TOKENS overrides), and the
# summary reports per arm how many turns got past </think>, made a tool call and finished stop or length. The pre-registered random order
# trims the arms that do not fit their share of the box.
# reset first: the window's earlier jobs (T5 is the last that can wedge a board) leave the ring fabric up.
# C2_TAULAB_DATA is rig-local and READ ONLY to the job (the default is kwork64/taulab/data under the runner's home); its files are
# checked against MANIFEST.json and the arm counts BEFORE the container starts (a shortfall refuses the job). The results, the container's
# log and the driver's own log are written under kwork64/taulab/ and never uploaded: the uploaded artifact holds
# taulab/tau-lab-summary.json, aggregates only (the Qwen repo, its logs and artifacts are public). C2_TAULAB_COUNTERS: production's
# spec-decode counters (a JSON of aggregates, positions 1-3 are compared within +/-10%); production is not served tonight, so leave it
# unset and that check reads NOT_ESTABLISHED (reason no_production_counters: a known gap).
# C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE: 270 min for the whole run, the container load (about 10 min) included; the driver gives each arm the time left in
# proportion to the wall estimates (A1 85, A2 55, A3 8, A4 60, A5 20 min) and keeps 15 min for the stop and the report. A hang is
# bounded: a request waits 10 min at most, four consecutive transport failures or a vanished container stop the lab, a canary after the
# first turns requires [PACKED] rounds and phase records in the log, and the step is killed 20 min past the deadline. A run killed
# mid-way RESUMES when its workflow run is re-run (the results directory is keyed by the run id: the turns already done are skipped),
# and the report reruns over any results directory (c2_tau_lab.py --analyze-only).
# Duration (estimate): 275 min (card time 4.5 h). Stop rule: none (optional); a refusal before the container starts costs nothing.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-2
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A4 A5
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=120
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
